# An ALLOWLIST, not a denylist, because a denylist is one forgotten line away from baking a
# credential into an image. `exulanica/models/credentials.py` walks up from the process working
# directory looking for a `.env` file, so a `.env` that reaches /app is a credential the image
# carries, which `docs/deployment.md` forbids. It is excluded here structurally rather than by a
# rule somebody has to remember to add.
#
# It is also the difference between a build context of about 1.5 GB and one of a few megabytes:
# `.venv`, `web/node_modules`, `.orimera` and `.exulanica` are the bulk of this checkout and the
# image needs none of them.
*
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!LICENSE
!THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md
!exulanica
# The gsplat trainer recipe under deploy/gsplat is its own build; it needs only its pinned
# requirements from this directory.
!deploy/gsplat/requirements.txt
